WEBVTT

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.060
Oh, Warwick!

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.060
My father is...

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.270
His dukedom may live on in me,

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.280
but he is no longer with us!

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.900
Edward.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.450
If you are his son,
then do not stop at a dukedom.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.410
Call yourself a king.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.620
Claim the crown, or you are
no child of Richard Plantagenet!

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:44.410
Warwick.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:49.130
My troops will acclaim
you King of England.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:52.800
London has barred its gates
against the Lancastrians.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.470
That will force them to withdraw for now.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:59.260
We'll end this war then.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:03.180
Gentlemen, this next battle
will shape our future.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.600
All those who love England, follow me!

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.190
My father called you
the "savior of his soul."

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:14.690
I feel as he did, Warwick.

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:18.320
Let us vow to chain our souls together.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.580
When you fall, so shall I!

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:25.460
I have no need of tears.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:28.500
Our mourning clothes are steel chains.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.250
We'll bring our swords of vengeance
down on Lancastrian helms!

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.340
O Lord, grant us strength!

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.430
No matter how much I weep,

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:42.100
merely breathing is enough
to stoke the fires of my rage

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.390
and burn my body to ashes.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.730
York of the white rose.

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:55.240
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:01.780
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:06.500
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:57.900
Warwick.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:01.860
I'm sorry.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:08.030
I swore to my beloved that I would
be with her if I returned alive.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:12.160
You should not say such things,
even in jest.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.330
I never jest.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:19.300
And right now, I'm "with" you, Warwick.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.550
Where am I?

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.810
What am I doing?

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:38.860
Everywhere I look is pitch dark.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.400
Fire!

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.280
I can no longer...

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:51.330
see any color but the red of blood.

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:59.340
How many of them can we
kill before they close with us?

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:02.260
The will of heaven will decide the rest.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.100
What do I desire?

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:17.440
Tears cannot quench the fires
that consume me.

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:32.660
Go! Crush the Yorkists in a single charge!

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:37.420
Leave this to me! Fall back and--

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.500
I swore to stand with you, Warwick!

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:40.750
In heaven's name!

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:45.840
Look, Warwick. Look at the sun.

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:06.650
Blood! It's blood that I need!

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:09.570
More! More! More!

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:11.030
I want more blood!

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.870
Enemy reinforcements?!

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.160
Yes, they number in the thousands.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.920
Our men's morale will inevitably suffer.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:23.710
Might I suggest we retreat
while we still can?

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:32.300
That sun is a good omen!

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.140
Heaven sides with us!

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:37.520
Now is the time to avenge my father!

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.520
The world is dark.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:43.360
I have been forever robbed of light.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:47.070
In the dark, I can see
only the color of blood.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:49.280
So, I will cover the world...

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.450
In blood! Blood! Blood!

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:52.530
Blood!

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.830
I'll color it with blood!

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:14.390
Are you a Lancastrian?

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:20.350
Help me. I can't move.

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:22.270
Please.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:24.360
My family's waiting for me.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:28.900
I can't see.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:33.030
I don't recognize your face.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:35.200
Will you color it for me?

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.040
Color the world?

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:40.040
I'm sure that I'll be able to see then.

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:06.560
Yes. Even without light,

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:10.650
all that my eyes see--the whole
world--will be in color.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:15.740
It won't be dark anymore.

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:30.920
Hey, this one's breathing.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:32.720
So kill him.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:36.390
I know, but his rose is so bloody
I can't tell if it's white or--

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:38.430
Wait a moment.

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:39.680
I know him.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:49.320
I'm amazed you recognized me.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:52.530
I've known you ever since you were born.

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:55.570
Simply to be at your side.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:09:00.450
That is the role assigned to me in life.

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:03.540
You needn't feel bound by loyalty.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:06.960
My father is no longer of this world.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:12.510
And so, I resigned my post
and went in search of you.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:17.050
In order to deliver you
into your mother's arms.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:22.640
Officially, you fled along with your
lady mother and Lord George.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.890
That is as it must be.

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:27.940
Your father would want it that way.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:35.360
Yes, you're right.

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:38.820
I'm sure that's what Father would want.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:41.830
I am the shadow,

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:44.370
the darkness behind the light.

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:47.830
As your king, I now declare to you:

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:50.670
We have won! Victory is ours!

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:52.670
Long live King Edward!

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:57.130
But that's fine.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:02.010
I'll go on walking alone,
even in the dark.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:06.140
I've found a way to do it.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:37.760
Are you <i>still </i>dressing, Richard?!

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:43.100
Pardon me, George.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:48.270
Richard, you're always nearly late because
you won't let servants help you.

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:51.020
It was never a problem with Catesby.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:59.400
That was two years ago.
He no longer serves the House of York.

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:03.870
Oh, yeah. He's with
Lord Hastings now, isn't he?

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.830
King Edward is here!

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:12.500
His Majesty's beauty always astounds me.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:16.380
I know! You'd think he
was born to be king.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:20.970
And that's the "Kingmaker,"
the Earl of Warwick.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:24.600
The Yorkists would never have
emerged victorious without him.

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:28.520
Lord George and Lord Richard
have grown handsome as well.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:31.690
But Lord Richard rather frightens me.

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:33.610
He seems so unapproachable.

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:36.480
Now that the crown of victory is ours,

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:40.860
battle-scarred armor has
been reduced to decoration.

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:43.110
George! Richard!

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:47.700
Richard, I'm told that you've barred
servants from your chambers.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:50.500
You are the Duke of Gloucester now.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:54.250
You cannot rule without
your people's trust.

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:55.920
Forgive me.

00:11:55.920 --> 00:12:00.010
I am ashamed to expose
my frail body to their sight.

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:05.300
You are slender, and your skin
is as smooth as a maiden's.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.260
But you needn't be ashamed.

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:10.930
Such trifles don't determine
a man's worth.

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:13.520
What does determine it, then?

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:16.940
Women.

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:20.610
My brothers, do any of
these strike your fancies?

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:23.110
They are all lovely ladies.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:26.700
Wh-Why don't you court them, then?

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:30.910
I'm already promised to a lady in France.

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:34.080
Warwick is formally pursuing
the engagement.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:39.130
My brothers, your king commands you!

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:43.260
Choose partners for today from
among these maidens here!

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:47.260
What should we do, Richard?
I know you hate this sort of thing.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:49.140
It's just for this party.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:51.600
His Majesty will be satisfied
once we choose.

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:56.230
You know, you've changed a little.

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:58.860
Ever since Father died.

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:01.820
I'm not a child anymore.

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:04.740
Come on. Let's put ourselves
in the running.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:06.660
I-I'll stay out of it.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:09.080
I'm not good with men.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:11.240
Oh, honestly, Anne.

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:14.790
I know that you can't
stop thinking about--

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.330
I said I don't want to!

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:18.340
You can join in on your own!

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:22.010
Oh, my.

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:25.630
Anne Neville.

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:27.140
Lord Richard!

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:29.640
Um, I-I'm...

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:31.350
I'm sorry about before!

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:33.520
I wanted to apologize.

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:36.770
I realized that I might have said
something awful to you.

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:39.610
I really didn't mean to.

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:44.530
I hoped that you and I could be, um...

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.450
...friends.

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:52.370
Anne, give me your hand.

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:58.960
Where did that come from?!

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:04.050
If Lord Richard is with my sister,
then you must be my partner!

00:14:14.350 --> 00:14:17.810
I was right, Warwick.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:21.230
Your daughters have grown quite beautiful.

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:23.900
I envy my brothers.

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:28.530
I trust that my French lady
is quite the beauty as well.

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:31.160
Leave everything to me.

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:35.870
I plan to do nothing
without your approval.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:39.370
The two of us won this throne together.

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:40.380
Wait!

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:45.170
Your Royal Majesty, I beg of you.

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:47.050
This is a celebration.

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:48.220
I will hear business during--

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:51.680
I have made many requests
these past two years,

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:55.220
yet I was never granted an audience.

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:59.270
I beg Your Majesty to return
my late husband's lands,

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:01.440
which were confiscated in the war.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:03.150
Confiscated?

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:07.570
That would make your late husband
a Lancastrian, I presume.

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:11.490
Interesting. You're a courageous woman.

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:12.780
What's your name?

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:13.780
Your Majesty.

00:15:16.830 --> 00:15:19.830
I am called Elizabeth Woodville.

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:27.880
Very well. I will hear your petition.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:31.470
But not during a banquet. Leave us.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:41.980
Your Majesty, as I was saying about your
engagement to the French lady...

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:46.940
Elizabeth Woodville.

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:49.610
Where have I...?

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:52.410
Show yourself.

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:55.830
I made you tremble with fear as a child,

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:58.790
but you're used to me now.

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:00.960
What's so funny?

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.420
Have you fallen in love?

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:05.210
With the beautiful Elizabeth?

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:06.130
Nonsense.

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:08.340
But she's in your thoughts.

00:16:08.340 --> 00:16:10.590
Charming little Anne.

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:12.220
I don't fall in love.

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:14.930
You could never get her
to love you back, anyway.

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:18.430
Not with your body.

00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:19.560
Enough!

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:21.690
I'm joking.

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:25.610
After all, your affections lie elsewhere.

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:29.730
Richard, you are neither
a man nor a woman,

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:33.320
but you are also both a man <i>and </i>a woman.

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:41.580
I won't love anyone.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:42.660
Anyone at all.

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:48.250
Queen Margaret! King Henry's spirit
has at last returned to him!

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:54.380
Where... Where am I?

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:57.550
In Scotland.

00:16:57.550 --> 00:17:00.430
Those abominable Yorkists
seized the throne,

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:05.230
and forced us, the rightful royal family,
into exile in a foreign land.

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:09.320
The war is over.

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:11.320
What a deplorable state of affairs!

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:16.320
I'm no longer king.

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:19.780
I'm free. Free!

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:24.580
What's gotten into you, Edward?

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:26.120
Why a hunting trip?

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:29.630
It's nice to hunt without
a crowd once in a while.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:31.880
Look, my brothers.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:36.090
That day, I saw the sun
above the snowy battlefield.

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:38.800
That single sun split into three,

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:41.140
and then rejoined into one.

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:44.480
The three suns are us three brothers.

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:50.480
It was a divine revelation commanding
us to rule this land in concert.

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:54.360
We three York brothers
are under the sun's aegis.

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:58.740
Let us strengthen our bonds
by hunting under this sun's light.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:03.660
Now, we'll see which of us can
bring down the largest game!

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.750
He's certainly in a good mood.

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:21.510
I long to see you.

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:28.940
I trust you've read my letter,

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:30.230
Elizabeth?

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:35.650
Yes. You wrote that you would
return my husband's lands.

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:39.070
And in exchange, I ask for your love.

00:18:39.070 --> 00:18:41.070
I believe I wrote as much.

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:44.410
Your Royal Majesty,
as I am an English subject,

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:47.160
my love has always been yours.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:51.790
Elizabeth, it is the fruits
of love that I desire.

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:53.210
Put plainly,

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:57.340
I want to sleep with you.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:02.470
Then Your Majesty must send me
to sleep in a prison cell.

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:09.940
You would slay a king
to preserve your honor?

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:13.520
I would.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:18.110
You're the first woman
who has ever refused me.

00:19:18.110 --> 00:19:22.070
Elizabeth, I'm more eager
to test you than ever.

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:29.870
Your Majesty, I am too lowly
to be your queen,

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:33.670
but I am too noble to be your mistress.

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:38.510
My queen? You're bolder than
your gentle looks suggest.

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:41.510
How amusing.

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:44.930
Would you be my queen, Elizabeth?

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:51.770
Those who love Your Majesty
would never permit it.

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:56.480
Elizabeth, you are the only one I love.

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:58.570
I'll hear no more refusals.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:04.530
I am king, and I have made my decision.

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:12.960
So, this is why he
suddenly wanted to hunt.

00:20:24.510 --> 00:20:25.640
You saw us.

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:30.560
For the present, this secret
stays just between us.

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:33.560
Richard,

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.150
I have decided...

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:38.690
...to make her my queen.

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:43.990
What is this letter?!

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:45.820
King Edward and his Yorkists killed your--

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:46.910
Anthony...

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:52.410
Do you know what this is?

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:55.380
It's a memento of my husband.

00:20:55.380 --> 00:21:00.010
I still love only one man.

00:21:00.010 --> 00:21:02.760
And so, I will avenge him.

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:06.260
I'll become queen,
bend the king to my will,

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:11.600
and the Royal Family of York,
my husband's killers, will be ours.

00:21:14.310 --> 00:21:17.900
Edward's French marriage
will bring even greater power

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:21.280
to the Royal Family of York.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:25.950
Your son looks more
like you than ever lately.

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:28.870
Sometimes I mistake him for you,

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:29.780
Your Majesty.

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:36.710
I promise to defend your crown,

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:40.000
no matter who threatens it.

00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:55.230
Hey, have you heard?

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:58.900
They say King Edward comes hunting here.

00:21:58.900 --> 00:22:00.150
Incognito?

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:03.610
Of course. I mean, this <i>is </i>King Edward.

00:22:03.610 --> 00:22:06.320
You hide your wives and
daughters when he comes by.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:08.870
Excuse me.

00:22:08.870 --> 00:22:10.780
I'm looking for someone.
